 "notes": "Rows 68v l.13 (image 0084_0141) and 69r l.1-5 (image 0084_0142): 14 + 13 + 13 + 15 + 13 + 13 = 81, as the record. The coarser copy on 68v l.14 is not counted. Plain 1.4x half-line zooms and 2x crops of each line in thirds (y_*.png). The words the record reads securely (فتنتني, غبث, في, غنث, خفيف, خففت, جفتني, ضجث, فتنث, ذبث, غزتني) give a key with no conflict except ٣ = ت and ث; with it the other groups read as listed (by-eye key, not independently confirmed): بجنبي (\"at my side\", record نخبي), جيبي (record جبي), تجنبتني (7 signs, record تجنبني), and four words of the shape ـيبي where the record has ـبي. The first word, ٣ 8 6 ω ٣, gives ث ن غ ب ت (record ثقبت): the 8-loop is ن in فتنتني, غنث, بجنبي, تجنبتني, جفتني, فتنث, غزتني, بينث, and no other sign stands for ق; keyed as ثنغبت (ت/ث by the record). بتنث is بينث in the cipher. The ٣ writing ت and ث is the encipherer's merging of a look-alike pair (the compiler's تشابه), so ت/ث per word is taken from the reading."
